Grandma’s Story: The Mango Tree (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100152

Grandma smiled and said, “Let me tell you a story.”

“Long ago, in a small village, there was a little boy named Ravi.

In his backyard stood a big mango tree.

Every day, Ravi played under the tree.

He climbed its branches, ate its sweet mangoes, and rested in its shade.

As Ravi grew older, he stopped visiting the tree.

One day, he returned and said, ‘I need money.’

The tree said, ‘Take my mangoes and sell them.’

Ravi took them and left.

Years passed.

Ravi came back again and said, ‘I need a house.’

The tree said, ‘Cut my branches and build one.’

Ravi did so and left again.

After many years, Ravi returned as an old man.

‘I am tired. I just need a place to rest,’ he said.

The tree, now only a stump, said softly, ‘Sit here and rest.’

Grandma looked at the children and said, ‘The tree was like our parents—always giving.’”

💖 Moral:

Parents always give selflessly—respect and care for them.